    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6e608c85-7522-53a3-9884-8a9ae6b25d75",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A$ below. Which set of entries should be replaced by $0$ to obtain row echelon form **using the fewest replacements**? Leave all other entries unchanged.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The minimum set is $a_{21}$, $a_{31}$, and $a_{33}$. Replace these 3 entries with $0$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ -8 & 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\longrightarrow\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe nonzero rows have leading entries in columns 2, 3, 4, in strictly increasing order, and all zero rows are at the bottom. \n\nRestoring $a_{21}$ would put the leading entry of row 2 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 1. Restoring $a_{31}$ would put the leading entry of row 3 in column 1, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 2. Restoring $a_{33}$ would put the leading entry of row 3 in column 3, which is not to the right of the leading entry in row 2. No set with fewer than 3 replacements satisfies both the leading-entry order and zero-row conditions.\n\nEntries to the right of a leading entry may remain nonzero.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "3210ca01-1392-5135-8a13-e4ef87d1df92",
